<h1>How we handle your email</h1>

<p class="meta">
  Last updated <time datetime="{{ page.date | isoDate }}">{{ page.date | readableDate }}</time>
</p>

<h2>What we collect</h2>
<p>
  If you subscribe, we store your email address. That is the only personal
  information we ask you for. We do not ask for your name, and there is no account to
  create.
</p>
<p>
  Our email provider{% if newsletter.provider %}, {{ newsletter.provider }},{% endif %}
  stores your address on our behalf and records the date you confirmed your
  subscription, plus whether recent emails to you bounced. That last part is how we
  stop sending to dead addresses.
</p>

<h2>What we do with it</h2>
<p>
  We use your address to send you our own writing. Nothing else. We do not sell it,
  rent it, trade it, or hand it to advertisers, and we do not send you other people's
  promotions.
</p>
<p>
  We never add an address that was not typed into our own form and then confirmed by
  clicking a link in an email. We do not buy lists, and we do not treat a business
  card, a reply, or a follow as permission.
</p>

<h2>Leaving</h2>
<p>
  Every email we send carries an unsubscribe link. One click removes you — no reply
  needed, no reason required, no “are you sure” page. If the link ever fails, email us
  and we will remove you by hand.
</p>

<h2>The rest of the site</h2>
<p>
  These pages are static files. There are no advertising cookies, no ad networks, and
  no web fonts, so reading here does not require you to trust anyone but us and our
  host.
</p>

<h2>How we count readers</h2>
<p>
  We do want to know which pieces people actually read, so we run our own copy of
  <a href="https://umami.is/">Umami</a> on our own server. Nothing about it is shared
  with anyone else.
</p>
<p>
  For each page view it records the page you opened, the site that linked you here,
  your country, and the sort of browser and device you used. On an article it also
  records two facts about your visit: whether you scrolled to the end, and whether the
  page stayed open and visible for thirty seconds.
</p>
<p>What it does not do:</p>
<ul>
  <li>It sets no cookies and stores nothing on your device. That is why this site
    has no consent banner to click past.</li>
  <li>It does not keep your IP address. Your address is scrambled together with your
    browser details and a code that changes daily, purely so that reading two pages in
    one afternoon counts as one person rather than two. The result cannot be turned
    back into an address, and it stops matching you tomorrow.</li>
  <li>It cannot follow you to other websites, and there is nothing here for an
    advertiser to buy.</li>
  <li>It has no idea who you are. Even if you subscribe by email, we cannot connect
    your address to anything you read — the two never meet.</li>
  <li>It does not record your screen, your mouse, or your keystrokes.</li>
  <li>If your browser sends a Do Not Track signal, we count nothing at all.</li>
</ul>
